#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:2
msgid "Loading tasks from another file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:4
msgid ""
"There are some scenarios where one might wish to define tasks outside of "
"pyproject.toml, or to collect tasks from multiple projects into one. For "
"example, if you want to share tasks between projects via git modules, "
"generate tasks definitions dynamically, organize your code in a monorepo, or "
"simply have a lot of tasks and don't want the pyproject.toml to get too "
"large. This can be achieved by creating a toml, yaml, or json file including "
"the same structure for tasks as used in pyproject.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:8
msgid ""
"Imported toml, yaml, or json files are not required to namespace config "
"under ``tool.poe``. However if config exists under this structure then it "
"will be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:10
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:12
msgid "./pyproject.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:12
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"include = \"modules/acme_common/shared_tasks.toml\" # include tasks from a "
"git submodule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:18
msgid "./modules/acme_common/shared_tasks.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:18
msgid ""
"[tool.poe.tasks.build-image]\n"
"cmd = \"docker build\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:24
msgid ""
"Imported files may also specify environment variables via ``tool.poe."
"envfile`` or entries for ``tool.poe.env``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:29
msgid ""
"If a referenced file is missing then poe ignores it without error, though "
"failure to read the contents will result in failure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:32
msgid "Disabling recursion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:34
msgid ""
"By default, includes are followed recursively. You can disable this for a "
"specific include by setting ``recursive = false``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:36
msgid ""
"[[tool.poe.include]]\n"
"path = \"external/tasks.toml\"\n"
"recursive = false"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:42
msgid ""
"When ``recursive`` is ``false``, the included file's own tasks and "
"environment variables are still loaded, but any ``include`` entries within "
"that file are not followed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:46
msgid "Including tasks from a python package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:48
msgid ""
"You can also include tasks from a python function originating either within "
"the current project or from a dependency. This makes it much easier to share "
"tasks across projects by distributing them as a python package, or to "
"dynamically generate tasks depending on the context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:50
msgid ""
"For more details see the :doc:`include_script<../guides/packaged_tasks>` "
"global option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:52
msgid ""
"The ``include_script`` option is ignored in included files due to the "
"complexity of coordinating executors (for loading the scripts) across config "
"files. So ``include_script`` can only be used in the main pyproject.toml "
"file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:56
msgid "Including multiple files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:58
msgid ""
"It's also possible to include tasks from multiple files by providing a list "
"like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:60
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"include = [\"modules/acme_common/shared_tasks.toml\", \"generated_tasks."
"json\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:65
msgid ""
"Files are loaded in the order specified. If an item already exists then the "
"included value is ignored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:67
msgid ""
"Included files can themselves include other files, and these will be loaded "
"before the parent file is loaded. Therefore if there are multiple includes "
"then they are loaded depth first in the order specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:71
msgid "Setting a working directory for included tasks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:73
msgid ""
"When including files from another location, you can also specify that tasks "
"from that other file should be run from within a specific directory. For "
"example with the following configuration, when tasks imported from "
"*my_subproject* are run from the root, the task will actually execute as if "
"it had been run from the *my_subproject* subdirectory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:75
msgid ""
"[[tool.poe.include]]\n"
"path = \"my_subproject/pyproject.toml\"\n"
"cwd  = \"my_subproject\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:81
msgid ""
"The directory indicated by the ``cwd`` option will also be used as the base "
"directory for global or task level ``envfile`` imports for tasks defined "
"within an included file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:83
msgid ""
"Tasks and config in an included file can access the ``cwd`` value via the "
"``POE_CONF_DIR`` environment variable. When no ``cwd`` is set on the include "
"then ``POE_CONF_DIR`` refers to the parent directory of the config file "
"where a task is defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:85
msgid ""
"You can still specify that an envfile referenced within an included file "
"should be imported relative to the main project root, using the ``POE_ROOT`` "
"environment variable like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:87
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"envfile = \"${POE_ROOT}/.env\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:94
msgid "Including files relative to the git repo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:96
msgid ""
"Normally include paths are resolved relative to the project root (that is "
"the parent directory of the pyproject.toml). However when working with a "
"monorepo it can also be useful to specify the file to include relative to "
"the root of the git repository, which can be done by referenceing the "
"``POE_GIT_DIR`` or ``POE_GIT_ROOT`` variables like so:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:98
msgid ""
"[tool.poe]\n"
"include = \"${POE_GIT_DIR}/tasks.toml\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guides/include_guide.rst:103
msgid ""
"See the documentation on :ref:`Special variables<Special variables>` for a "
"full explanation of how these variables work."
msgstr ""
